    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n5849" root="جشر" body-key="j">
    
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">جَشَّارٌ</span></b>  The <i>owner</i> (<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">صَاحِب</span>) <i>of a pasture-land in
which horses feed.</i> (K.) You say, "He is the
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">جَشَّار</span> of our camels." (A, TA. [But it seems
to be implied in the A that it signifies the same
as <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">جَاشِرٌ</span> as explained below.])

  </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
